DocAlign
A documentation portfolio project by Martha Wood
DocAlign is a self-directed portfolio project expploring how documentation can be kept reliable, accurate, and maintainable through automated, AI-assisted analysis integratedf into CI/CD pipelines, bringing a "code-quality" mindset to technical documentation.

DocAlign and its parent company, Covalent Technologies, are fictional. 

This project was created to demonstrate technical writing, documentation design, and docs-as-code practices. 
Any resemblance to real companies or products is coincidental.
